   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{}},
  :1-l6a002
  {:statement
   "For each $\\omega \\in \\Omega$, let $k_\\omega \\geq 1$ be a positive integer. Define $\\Omega' = \\bigsqcup_{\\omega \\in \\Omega} \\{(\\omega, j) : j \\in [k_\\omega]\\}$ and distribution $\\pi'(\\omega, j) = \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega}$ for each $j \\in [k_\\omega]$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "782a557881375273",
   :display-order 2,
   :type :assumption,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :assumption,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l6a002,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l6a001}},
  :1-l6a003
  {:statement
   "We verify $\\pi'$ is a probability distribution: $\\sum_{(\\omega,j) \\in \\Omega'} \\pi'(\\omega,j) = \\sum_{\\omega \\in \\Omega} \\sum_{j=1}^{k_\\omega} \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} = \\sum_{\\omega \\in \\Omega} \\pi(\\omega) = 1$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "2d13cca6ddf8c074",
   :display-order 3,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l6a003,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l6a002}},
  :1-l6a004
  {:statement
   "Compute the entropy of $\\pi'$: $H(\\pi') = -\\sum_{(\\omega,j) \\in \\Omega'} \\pi'(\\omega,j) \\log_2 \\pi'(\\omega,j) = -\\sum_{\\omega \\in \\Omega} \\sum_{j=1}^{k_\\omega} \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} \\log_2 \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega}$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "ac39e15f03f34b76",
   :display-order 4,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :definition-expansion,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l6a004,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l6a002}},
  :1-l6a005
  {:statement
   "Using $\\log_2 \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} = \\log_2 \\pi(\\omega) - \\log_2 k_\\omega$, we get: $H(\\pi') = -\\sum_{\\omega} \\sum_{j=1}^{k_\\omega} \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} (\\log_2 \\pi(\\omega) - \\log_2 k_\\omega) = -\\sum_{\\omega} \\sum_{j=1}^{k_\\omega} \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} \\log_2 \\pi(\\omega) + \\sum_{\\omega} \\sum_{j=1}^{k_\\omega} \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} \\log_2 k_\\omega$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "743cb99d51d023d3",
   :display-order 5,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l6a005,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l6a004}},
  :1-l6a006
  {:statement
   "Sum over $j$ first. For the first term: $\\sum_{j=1}^{k_\\omega} \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} = \\pi(\\omega)$, so $-\\sum_{\\omega} \\sum_j \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} \\log_2 \\pi(\\omega) = -\\sum_{\\omega} \\pi(\\omega) \\log_2 \\pi(\\omega) = H(\\pi)$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "ef4733a51d7655bc",
   :display-order 6,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l6a006,
   :provenance
   {:created-at "2026-01-06T18:00:00Z",
    :created-by :prover,
    :round 1,
    :revision-of nil},
   :depth 1,
   :dependencies #{:1-l6a005 :1-l6a001}},
  :1-l6a007
  {:statement
   "For the second term: $\\sum_{j=1}^{k_\\omega} \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} \\log_2 k_\\omega = \\pi(\\omega) \\log_2 k_\\omega$ (summing $k_\\omega$ identical terms), so $\\sum_{\\omega} \\sum_j \\frac{\\pi(\\omega)}{k_\\omega} \\log_2 k_\\omega = \\sum_{\\omega} \\pi(\\omega) \\log_2 k_\\omega = \\mathbb{E}_\\pi[\\log_2 k_\\omega]$.",
   :taint :clean,
   :parent nil,
   :content-hash "72dbe405272e119f",
   :display-order 7,
   :type :claim,
   :scope #{},
   :justification :algebraic-rewrite,
   :status :verified,
   :id :1-l6a007,
